#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/all-about-interfaces.md:0
msgid ""
"Understand snap interfaces, which give confined snaps access to system "
"resources and other snaps using plugs and slots, either automatically or "
"manually."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/all-about-interfaces.md:8
msgid "All about interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/all-about-interfaces.md:10
msgid ""
"By default, snaps with strict confinement are only able to access a limited "
"set of resources outside the environment they run in. Snaps can only access "
"resources from the system and other snaps via interfaces that describe the "
"resources they provide."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/all-about-interfaces.md:12
msgid ""
"The creator of a snap selects the interfaces that a snap requires in order "
"to function correctly. Common interfaces include those that provide access "
"to the {ref}`network <interfaces-network-interface>`, {ref}`desktop features "
"<interfaces-desktop-interface>` and {ref}`audio recording <interfaces-audio-"
"record-interface>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/all-about-interfaces.md:14
msgid "Connecting interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/all-about-interfaces.md:16
msgid ""
"A connection between snaps is made when a plug from a snap needing a "
"resource is connected to a slot in another snap providing that resource. A "
"analogy to this is plugging an appliance into an electrical outlet that "
"provides the power it needs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/all-about-interfaces.md:21
msgid ""
"![How an interfaces uses a plug and a slot](https://assets.ubuntu.com/"
"v1/59c290a8-snapd-interfaces.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/all-about-interfaces.md:21
msgid "How an interfaces uses a plug and a slot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/all-about-interfaces.md:23
msgid ""
"Connections are made either automatically at install time or manually, "
"depending on their function. The desktop interface is connected "
"automatically, for instance, whereas the camera interface is not. The *Auto-"
"connect* column in the {ref}`Supported interfaces <ref-index_interfaces>` "
"table for lists  whether an interface automatically connects or not. See the "
"{ref}`Interface Auto-connection mechanism <explanation-interfaces-interface-"
"auto-connection>` for implementation details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/all-about-interfaces.md:25
msgid ""
"As with {ref}`classic confinement <explanation-security-classic-"
"confinement>`, a snap's publisher can request an *assertion* to "
"automatically connect an otherwise non-auto-connecting interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/all-about-interfaces.md:27
msgid ""
"If a snap is upgraded and includes a new assertion, the user will still need "
"to connect the interface manually. Similarly, if an installed classic snap "
"is upgraded to use strict confinement, its interfaces won't be automatically "
"configured."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/all-about-interfaces.md:29
msgid ""
"If a snap is installed prior to an interface being granted auto-connect "
"permission, and permission is subsequently granted and the snap updated, "
"when the installed snap updates, the interface will be auto-connected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/all-about-interfaces.md:31
msgid "Getting the interfaces for a snap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/all-about-interfaces.md:33
msgid ""
"Use the `snap connections` command to see which interfaces a snap needs, and "
"which are currently connected:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/all-about-interfaces.md:35
msgid ""
"$ snap connections vlc\n"
"Interface         Plug                  Slot               Notes\n"
"camera            vlc:camera            -                  -\n"
"desktop           vlc:desktop           :desktop           -\n"
"desktop-legacy    vlc:desktop-legacy    :desktop-legacy    -\n"
"home              vlc:home              :home              -\n"
"mount-observe     vlc:mount-observe     -                  -\n"
"[...]\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/all-about-interfaces.md:46
msgid ""
"In the above example,  we can see that the `vlc:camera` interface is "
"disconnected because it has an empty *Slot* entry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/all-about-interfaces.md:48
msgid ""
"See {ref}`Interface management <how-to-guides-work-with-snaps-connect-"
"interfaces>` for further interface details, including how to disconnect "
"interfaces and make manual connections, and {ref}`Security policy and "
"sandboxing <explanation-security-security-policies>` for more information on "
"how confinement is implemented."
msgstr ""
